--TEST--
a misspelled segment of a `propertyPath<T>` literal is underlined alone, not the whole string, because the checker reports it at that segment's span — `rule:ide/a-field-path-completes-one-segment-at-a-time`, `rule:types/property-path`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Customer {
    public string $name = "Ada";
}
class Order {
    public ?Customer $customer = null;
}
class Grid {
    public static function sortBy(propertyPath<Order> $column): string {
        return $column as string;
    }
}

echo Grid::sortBy("customer.nmae");
--REQUEST--
diagnostics
--EXPECT--
14:29-14:33 error E0405 `Customer` has no public property `$nmae`
